        <body>
            <div xml:id="d921">

                <pb facs="0721" n="605" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg605"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/13278.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Vice Consul Silliman to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico City</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-09-23T21:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 23, 1914, 9 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Immediate reply requested. Break between Villa and Carranza is now hopeless.
                    Villa in telegram to Carranza yesterday disowns him as First Chief and states
                    that he will not participate in convention. It is now expected that convention
                    will be held as announced. It will represent a large majority of the
                    Constitutionalist movement regardless of Villa and Zapata and will formulate a
                    provisional government that, it is hoped, will meet the approval of the United
                    States. The convention will be loyal to Carranza.</p>
                <p>Carranza, thinking that my presence might be of service at this time to Mexico
                    and the United States, has urgently requested that I go immediately to
                    Washington. He has placed a special train to the border at my disposal. After
                    consulting with the Brazilian Minister I assume all the responsibility and am
                    leaving Mexico tonight. Mr. Belt remains to represent me.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Silliman</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
